      "ACR appropriateness criteria rate ultrasound as usually appropriate for essentially every thyroid nodule scenario, and reserve thyroid scintigraphy for scenarios with confirmed or suspected thyrotoxicosis, where it is usually appropriate.",
      "A hyperfunctioning ('hot') nodule carries a well-established 96-99% negative predictive value for malignancy, a figure robust enough that current risk-stratification systems such as ACR TI-RADS are understood to apply primarily to nodules not already known to be autonomously functioning.",
